==== hyperbricks yaml {!{page}} ====
page:
  - type: hypermedia
  - route: text-html-tree

  - content:
      - type: tree

      - intro_html:
          - type: html
          - value: |
              <h1>YAML tree fixture</h1>

      - intro_text:
          - type: text
          - value: Text and HTML components can live in one ordered tree.
==== explainer ====
HYPERMEDIA can contain a named TREE child with ordered HTML and TEXT leaves.
==== expected json ====
{
  "@order": [
    "content"
  ],
  "@type": "<HYPERMEDIA>",
  "content": {
    "@order": [
      "intro_html",
      "intro_text"
    ],
    "@type": "<TREE>",
    "intro_html": {
      "@type": "<HTML>",
      "value": "<h1>YAML tree fixture</h1>\n"
    },
    "intro_text": {
      "@type": "<TEXT>",
      "value": "Text and HTML components can live in one ordered tree."
    }
  },
  "route": "text-html-tree"
}
==== expected output ====
<!DOCTYPE html><html><body><h1>YAML tree fixture</h1>
Text and HTML components can live in one ordered tree.</body></html>
